#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD1011 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE 82-RULE GENERATOR-WILDCARD POPULATION (Fix #331 finding; owner ruled 2026-08-22 that all 82 are BUCKET 1 - no rule edit - with a sample of fixtures owed by the closing lane; authored by Fix #340). These rules never carried the injected var_exists guard in rules/ (NonEmptyGuardInliner.isGeneratorWildcard excludes wildcard names), but WildcardExpander re-ran installNativeExpr on the EXPANDED rule, where the arm wrapped the now-concrete leaf - so before Fix #330 an absent primary column silenced them at runtime. With the arm retired the expanded leaf is a bare empty(X): absent = all-missing, TRUE on every row. The mirror of the absent-primary pin, on the same single expansion (root AVISIT off the declared AVISITN): the primary AVISIT column is again absent, but the SECONDARY is blank on every row, so not empty(AVISITN) is FALSE and the rule is correctly silent. Together with the invalid twin this shows the absent column alone never decides the verdict - the restricting conjunct does, which is why the 82 are bucket 1."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AVISITN type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 |
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 |
